00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.710 align:start position:0%
arnold and happy days the emperor in  mulan and of course mr miyagi in the  karate kid all of these roles and more  were portrayed by pat morita keep  watching to find out more about this  esteemed actor's lengthy career and his  life outside of acting  mr miyagi is a master of martial arts  he's such an impressive and affecting  mentor he managed to reach kids in the  real world the karate kid's popularity  is often cited as a primary force in the  rise of youth martial arts academies  however morita's childhood was spent far  from the world of strip mall karate  classes he actually suffered from a rare  disease and was told he'd never be able  to walk he spent almost a decade of his  life in a tv ward called the weimar  institute eventually morita received an  experimental treatment that worked  marina defied grim expectations and  overcame the worst case scenarios for  his disease  during his illness morita was often  totally immobilized in a full body cast  that ran from neck to thigh because of  this he spent much of his time staring  at the ceiling trying to come up with  ways to keep himself entertained this is  where morita developed his sense of  humor and comedic timing if it wasn't  for my disease i wouldn't be here today  the hardship of his childhood helped  form his personality and made him who he  was later in life when morita was  released from the hospital with his  disease in check he was reunited with  his family unfortunately the year was  1943 and morita's family were japanese  immigrants  he recalled being escorted by an fbi  agent to the gila river war relocation  center in arizona after a little over a  year spent there his family was  transported to california's thule lake  war relocation center burrito was too  young to understand why they were being  held morita's anger grew as he got older  and began to comprehend the truth of the  way his family was treated  after the war ended morita's family  opened a restaurant in sacramento sadly  his father passed away in 1956. morita  then took an office job to help support  his family after years of this work he  decided he needed to make a change  remarkably marita's sense of humor had  remained intact through all this tragedy  he started working as a stand-up  comedian  those crazy kids huh they eat at home  come here use the telephone no wonder  all the business in the toilet his birth  name was noriyuki morita but he used pat  morita as a stage name because pat was  such a popular name at the time part of  what makes mr miyagi such an effective  character in the karate kid is morita's  comedic timing and subtle humor stand-up  comedy which he embarked upon in the  early 1960s is where he honed that  particular talent morita was known for  his self-deprecating sense of humor he  would often make himself the butt of his  own jokes it wasn't long before marita  got a better chance to showcase his  talents  morita started landing a few bit parts  in film and television in the mid-1960s  they were often roles that would be seen  as problematic and stereotypical today  one of his first ever film roles was as  oriental number two in the musical  thoroughly modern millie morita quickly  started cropping up in sitcoms like the  cosby show and green acres two  particular roles helped him break more  into the mainstream morita landed the  role of arnold takahashi on happy days  and he had a recurring role as achoo on  sanford and son this mainstream success  actually led to a history-making moment  for marita it propelled him into a  starring role on mr t and tina as taro  takahashi this was one of tv's first  predominantly asian american sitcoms  unfortunately the show only lasted a few  episodes but it was an important moment  in marita's career and in tv history  in hindsight it's easy to look at a film  like the karate kid and identify pat  morita as perfect for the role of mr  miyagi he embodies the characters so  flawlessly that it's impossible to  imagine anyone else playing him however  marita traveled a long road to get to  the role that would make him a legend  jerry weintraub the producer behind the  karate kid wouldn't even entertain the  idea of morita playing the role  weintraub's reasoning was that morita  was a comedian and the role of miyagi  was too nuanced for a comic to handle  the director of the karate kid john  avaldson held a private audition with  morita which he recorded during a later  meeting with weintraub aveltson started  playing the tape without telling  weintrap what was going on the recorded  performance convinced weintraub that  morita might actually be able to handle  the role morita still had to audition  five different times before being cast  noriyuki morita was nominated for an  academy award for his performance ralph  macchio  showed up marita's career was taken to  new heights with his role as miyagi in  the karate kid and its sequels he was  even nominated for an oscar morita  continued to appear in guest spots on a  variety of television shows including  appearances on the fresh prince of bel  air murder she wrote and family matters  he started landing roles as a voice  actor as well children of the 1990s may  recall morita as the host of  britannica's tales around the world in  addition to his performance as the  emperor in disney's mulan a role he  reprised in the sequels and video games  like kingdom hearts 2.  he even had a posthumous guest role as  master udon on a 2006 episode of  spongebob squarepants marita mostly  stuck to guest appearances and film  roles after the karate kid but he  occasionally took recurring roles on  television for example morita was part  of the central cast of the kids show the  mystery files of shelby wu in the late  1990s he also played uncle pat on the  barney-esque adventures with kangarati  after a long and varied career morita  died of kidney failure in 2005 at the  age of 73 as fans went on to learn  morita's lifelong struggle with  alcoholism played a part in his death  marita's wife evelyn has said that she  was well aware of her husband's  addiction and that she knew it was only  a matter of time before it took him the  actor himself was aware of it too and  reportedly told his wife that he knew he  couldn't get over his addiction marita's  daughter ali has commented on her  father's addiction as well just like  evelyn she recognizes what a kind and  caring soul her father had underneath it  all she has also said that her father  struggled with being a washed-up movie  star following his karate kid's success  still as she argues marita managed to  earn a little place in history morita's  legacy lives on largely due to his  unforgettable performance as mr miyagi  few who have seen the karate kid can  forget miyagi's lessons to daniel  larusso and the film still plays a  significant role in pop culture the  netflix series cobra kai centers around  several prominent characters from the  franchise it features a scene in which  daniel visits miyagi's grave had morita  still been alive there is no doubt that  he would have made a triumphant return  to the series ralph macchio has said it  was important to him and the rest of the  cast and crew to pay tribute and he's  woven throughout our show morita may be  gone but he is a long way from being  forgotten  if you or anyone you know is struggling  with addiction issues help is available  visit the substance abuse and mental  health services administration website  or contact samhsa's national helpline at  1-800-662-help
 

